// app/Identity.xcconfig — the single tracked source of the app's identity.
//
// Editing the four values below rebrands the app on both platforms. XcodeGen
// (configFiles:), Tuist (.settings(configurations:)) and xcodebuild all read
// this file natively — there is no parser in between, which is what lets
// `xcodebuild -showBuildSettings` report these resolved values directly.
// bin/preflight-identity.rb refuses to generate a project if any of the four
// is missing or empty, and names the variable.
//
// The project's STRUCTURE — app/App.xcodeproj, the App-iOS / App-macOS
// schemes, the App*Tests targets, App.entitlements — is a constant and is
// not configured here. Scripts and workflows spell the constant; nothing
// derives a path from a value in this file.
//
// Format rules: values are UNQUOTED (quotes would land in the plist as
// literal characters); comments are `//`; the `#` below is a directive, not
// a comment.

// Feeds PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER on both app targets (one shared bundle id).
// The four test bundles derive theirs from this value with a fixed suffix.
BUNDLE_ID        = com.example.helloapp

// Feeds PRODUCT_NAME on the two APP targets only, through a per-target
// PRODUCT_NAME = $(APP_PRODUCT_NAME) in each manifest. Deliberately NOT a
// bare PRODUCT_NAME: a project-level PRODUCT_NAME leaks into every target —
// all four test bundles would take this name and the two iOS ones would
// collide at one path under Build/Products/. Tuist writes a per-target
// PRODUCT_NAME, so a bare one would also make the two generators disagree.
APP_PRODUCT_NAME = HelloApp

// Feeds CFBundleDisplayName — the name under the icon — on both platforms.
DISPLAY_NAME     = HelloApp

// Feeds NSHumanReadableCopyright — the Info.plist key, set directly in both
// manifests' plist blocks — on both platforms. Not through an INFOPLIST_KEY_*
// build setting: that reaches the bundle only under GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE =
// YES, which the app targets do not set (observed: the setting resolved in
// -showBuildSettings, the built iOS plist had no key). The © is U+00A9.
COPYRIGHT        = TODO Copyright © <year> <Your Org>. All rights reserved.

// The Apple Team ID (DEVELOPMENT_TEAM) lives in app/Local.xcconfig, which is
// gitignored and never tracked. `make bootstrap-fork` writes it from
// FASTLANE_TEAM_ID in .bootstrap.env; on a clone that has not run it, create it by
// hand — it is one line. On a clone
// without that file the include below is
// silent and DEVELOPMENT_TEAM is undefined — not empty, undefined: no line for
// it appears in -showBuildSettings at all, and Xcode's own message on macOS is
// nothing (the build succeeds ad-hoc signed). The named failure comes from
// `bin/preflight-identity.rb --require-team`, not from the build.
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
